        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-27T12:17:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do you have numbers of how much it improves things? I\u0027m a bit worried that the lookup will add fixed overhead that\u0027s not great.\n\nWhat cases in Graphite does this improve? Can we just cache the full buffer UAV/SRV on creation because these are used for `var\u003cstorage\u003e` that don\u0027t really have a size limit and would tend to bind the whole buffer every time?",
      "revId": "29209acedce8d3e805fabb39b6fe3e51c0da11be",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "23e69562_44a76763",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/d3d11/BufferD3D11.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 331,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003501
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-27T12:42:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I saw MotionMark\u0027s canvas arc\u0027s score being increased from 12k to 20k just by caching the SRV.\n\nFrom the profiler, it looks like 21% of CPU time was spent in creating SRV (without caching) https://drive.google.com/file/d/1IMyWtxFf7iMoBpBAWLhExgAPenrZHeat/view?usp\u003dsharing\n\nI think the overhead of hash map is still much lower than creating SRV everytime.",
      "parentUuid": "8883db1b_e7b4f3f6",
      "revId": "29209acedce8d3e805fabb39b6fe3e51c0da11be",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "459a31b7_58c6379b",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/d3d11/BufferD3D11.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 331,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-27T13:10:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s surprisingly expensive indeed. But doesn\u0027t Graphite always use a complete view of the buffer?",
      "parentUuid": "23e69562_44a76763",
      "revId": "29209acedce8d3e805fabb39b6fe3e51c0da11be",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "52734031_c0553e92",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/d3d11/BufferD3D11.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 331,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003501
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-27T13:16:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For Canvas Arc test, mostly complete views are used. However,\nin Graphite, any offset and size could be used depending on the buffer manager class\u0027 decision. Hence, caching only full views seems like case specific optimization IMO. We want to avoid that and should make the code faster for every case. I would prefer graphite to not have some regressions in the wild reported on UMA that we don\u0027t know the exact scenarios.\n\nHow about we use a vector to store the views. For small number of views, vector should be faster than hash map. For large number of views, maybe we could use a limiting factor.",
      "parentUuid": "23e69562_44a76763",
      "revId": "29209acedce8d3e805fabb39b6fe3e51c0da11be",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "21f2c21b_3ab93be2",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/d3d11/BufferD3D11.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 331,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000283
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-27T17:49:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "flat_hash_map seems like the right type to use here, especially since your key is cheap to hash.\n\nI think if anything, we want to make sure these maps don\u0027t grow unbounded but the cost of an LRU on top of these is probably more overhead than we want.",
      "parentUuid": "52734031_c0553e92",
      "revId": "29209acedce8d3e805fabb39b6fe3e51c0da11be",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
